  "summary": "I wrote the trophy scene in `src/main.ts`, but I could not run it, and `vite build` has not been tried. `node_modules/@aura3d/` is empty in this sandbox, so `typecheck` fails with \"Cannot find module '@aura3d/engine'\". That is its only error. Every engine call is written from the docs in `llms.txt` and `docs/agents/`, with nothing checked against the real types. Nothing has been rendered, so lighting and exposure are untuned.\n\n- **Pedestal:** four stepped marble boxes, each face subdivided at about 2.5 cm. Marble colour comes from procedural 3D noise baked into vertex colours: turbulence-warped stripes in three vein scales over a cloudy white base. The material is physical with a clearcoat, so it should look polished and faintly reflective.\n- **Trophy:** a cup on a stem with a knop and two swept-tube handles, in polished gold (metallic 1, roughness 0.1). The cup, handles and a flat underside are built from generated profiles, with no external assets. Three bands in darker, rougher gold sit on the cup, knop and foot. The base is two tiers of black polished stone, with a thin gold plate and two engraved-looking lines on its front.\n- **Room and lights:** a dark warm room with bright cool and warm window panels and two lamps. `environments.capture` takes a reflection probe of the room for the gold to reflect. The key is a warm shadow-casting spotlight from above and in front, plus a faint cool fill, a cool rim light, a dim hemisphere light and a mild bloom.\n- **Camera and state:** the azimuth swings ±15° with a sine of about 20 s period. `window.__TASK_STATE__` is updated every frame, and `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()` and one animation frame.\n\nFour things could break at runtime, and a render check should look at each:\n- **Camera movement:** the docs do not give the argument shape for `app.camera.setPose`. I call it with `{ position, target }`. If it is missing or throws, the code rotates the pedestal and trophy group instead, so the view still swing",
